      <abstract>
<para>CPU shielding in &productname; isolates specific processors on a multi-core system exclusively for high-priority and real-time workloads. By using &systemd; and the cgroups v2 cpuset controller, administrators can isolate designated processors from standard system services and non-critical kernel threads. This isolation ensures deterministic execution times and eliminates latency spikes caused by resource contention, which is essential for real-time applications.</para>
<para><emphasis>Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>A multi-core system</para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Root or sudo privileges</para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
